何に追われ焦るのか?と笑う
Laughing, "What are we rushing and chasing after?"

394
00:40:29,164 --> 00:40:37,064
客観的に見てる私が嫌いだ
I hate myself for looking at it so objectively.

395
00:40:40,064 --> 00:40:46,564
決心のきっかけは 理屈ではなくて
The trigger for resolution isn't about logic,

396
00:40:47,264 --> 00:40:52,564
いつだってこの胸の衝動から始まる
it always starts from the impulse in my chest.

397
00:40:53,264 --> 00:40:59,864
流されてしまうこと 抵抗しながら
While resisting being carried away,

398
00:41:00,564 --> 00:41:08,064
生きるとは選択肢 たった一つを選ぶこと
living means choosing just one option.

399
00:41:10,164 --> 00:41:17,064
横断歩道 渡って いつも思う
Crossing the crosswalk, I always think,

400
00:41:17,264 --> 00:41:23,564
こんな風に 心に 信号があればいい
"If only there was a traffic light in my heart like this."

401
00:41:24,064 --> 00:41:29,864
進みなさい それから 止まりなさい
"Proceed, and then stop."

402
00:41:30,264 --> 00:41:36,864
それがルールならば 悩まずに行けるけれど…
If that were the rule, I could go without worrying...

403
00:41:38,064 --> 00:41:44,564
誰かの指示 待ち続けたくない
I don't want to keep waiting for someone else's instructions.

404
00:41:44,864 --> 00:41:50,864
走りたい時に 自分で踏み出せる
When I want to run, I want to take a step forward myself.

405
00:41:51,164 --> 00:41:57,564
強い意思を持った人でいたい
I want to be someone with a strong will.

406
00:41:58,064 --> 00:42:06,064
もう一人の明日の私を探そう
Let's search for another me of tomorrow.

407
00:42:09,164 --> 00:42:15,264
決心のきっかけは 時間切れじゃなくて
The trigger for resolution isn't running out of time,

408
00:42:15,864 --> 00:42:22,064
考えたその上で未来を信じること
but believing in the future after thinking it through.

409
00:42:22,564 --> 00:42:29,064
後悔はしたくない 思ったそのまま
I don't want to have any regrets, just as I thought.

410
00:42:29,864 --> 00:42:37,864
正解はわからない たった一度の人生だ
We don't know the right answer, it's a once-in-a-lifetime life.

411
00:42:39,964 --> 00:42:45,064
ほら 人ごみの誰かが走り出す
Look, someone in the crowd starts running,

412
00:42:45,864 --> 00:42:51,864
釣られたみたいにみんなが走り出す
everyone starts running as if dragged along.

413
00:42:52,564 --> 00:42:59,564
自分のこと 自分で決められず
Unable to decide things for myself,

414
00:43:00,064 --> 00:43:06,864
背中を押すもの 欲しいんだ
I want something to push my back.

415
00:43:07,264 --> 00:43:08,564
きっかけ
The trigger.

416
00:43:12,264 --> 00:43:18,564
決心のきっかけは 理屈ではなくて
The trigger for resolution isn't about logic,

417
